# Both spellings, deliberately. `.venv/` matches a directory and does NOT match a
# SYMLINK named `.venv`, which is how a worktree's link to the primary checkout's
# environment got committed here: an absolute path to one machine's home directory,
# tracked in a public repository, and a trap on every checkout of an older commit.
.venv
.venv/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
save.json
.coverage
coverage.xml
*.egg-info/
characters.json
accounts.json
codeforge.db
codeforge.db.bak*
*.db.bak*
.seedlab/
backups/
*.kdbx

# Dated security-patch audit reports (evidence trail; regenerated by `make patch`).
security-evidence/

# Dated ARC runtime-dimension verdicts (evidence trail; regenerated by `make arc-verdicts`).
arc-evidence/

# Exported runtime dependency set for the blocking CVE gate (regenerated by `make audit-runtime`).
runtime-requirements.txt

# Runtime Workshop outputs (generated, reproducible); keep the README tracked.
reports/*
!reports/README.md

# Generated cast sandbox (dry-run output; a cast becomes its own repo elsewhere)
casts/

# Local secrets/config: only .env.example (placeholders) is ever tracked.
.env

# Built docs site (regenerated by `make docs-build` / the Pages workflow).
site/

# The Foundry sandbox: generated candidate files (never promoted automatically).
workspace/

# The area bench: generated areas (reproducible from seed, mutable dev state); keep the README.
world_areas/*
!world_areas/README.md

# setuptools build artifacts (from a local pip install/build)
build/

# cosmic-ray mutation-testing session db (on-demand `make mutation`; reproducible from cosmic-ray.toml)
.cosmic-ray-session.sqlite

# Rust native extensions (build artifacts; keep Cargo.lock for reproducibility)
native/*/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Go service organs (the compiled edge binary; keep go.mod for reproducibility)
native/edge/codeforge-edge
# `go build ./...` names the binary after the MODULE, not the cmd. The pattern above only covered
# the named build, so a 3.4MB compiled binary was one `git add -A` from landing in history.
# gitignore has no trailing comments: a `#` on a pattern line becomes part of the pattern.
native/edge/edge

# Protocol spine: generated bindings (rebuilt via `make proto`; keep the .proto source + go.sum)
proto/telemetry_pb2.py
proto/*_pb2.pyi
native/spine/telemetrypb/
native/spine/xcheck/xcheck

# C text kernel (build artifacts; keep the source in native/textkernel/src)
native/textkernel/build/
native/textkernel/*.so
native/textkernel/*.egg-info/

# Runtime audit ledger (tamper-evident admin/economy log; reproducible, not tracked)
audit.jsonl

# Hypothesis local example cache (the COMMITTED corpus lives in tests/corpora/, tracked)
.hypothesis/

# Gradle daemon/cache state for the Rider projection. `build/` above already covers its
# output at any depth; this is the bit it does not.
.gradle/

# Gradle build output for the Rider projection. The WRAPPER is tracked (gradlew,
# gradle/wrapper/) so CI needs only a JDK; the caches and build dirs are not.
native/rider-retroforge/.gradle/
native/rider-retroforge/build/

# IntelliJ Platform plugin cache, created by the gradle-intellij-platform plugin the moment the
# L4 scaffold is configured. It is a downloaded IDE distribution and local metadata: large,
# regenerated on demand, and specific to one machine's plugin version. It has already surfaced
# once as a stranded-work FINDING on another bench, which is the honest reason this line exists:
# the ignore rule fixes the class, deleting it from one tree would have fixed one instance.
.intellijPlatform/

# Mutation-testing output. Regenerated by every `cargo mutants` run and worthless afterwards:
# it is a scratch build tree plus a report, not evidence. The report worth keeping goes in
# reports/, dated, like every other measurement.
mutants.out/
